[E0304] Error: cannot assign through a binding
    ╭─[ err/66_loop_errors/main.wip:10:9 ]
    │
  9 │     for x in xs {
    │         ┬  
    │         ╰── bound here
 10 │         x = 0
    │         ┬  
    │         ╰── `x` refers to part of a place that cannot be written
    │ 
    │ Help: bindings of `match` and `for` can be written when what they refer to can: a `var`, or a `&var` parameter
────╯
[E0322] Error: `break` outside a loop
    ╭─[ err/66_loop_errors/main.wip:15:5 ]
    │
 15 │     break
    │     ──┬──  
    │       ╰──── not inside `while` or `for`
    │ 
    │ Note: `break` leaves the innermost loop, and `continue` starts its next pass
────╯
[E0504] Error: cannot `continue` from a deferred expression
    ╭─[ err/66_loop_errors/main.wip:17:17 ]
    │
 17 │         defer { continue }
    │         ──┬──   ────┬───  
    │           ╰─────────────── inside this `defer`
    │                     │     
    │                     ╰───── would leave the loop in the middle of a block's cleanup
    │ 
    │ Note: a `defer` runs while its block exits, and cannot jump elsewhere; a loop written inside the deferred expression may use `break` and `continue`
────╯
[E0304] Error: cannot assign to `i`
