[E0323] Error: cannot iterate over `i64`
    ╭─[ err/66_loop_errors/main.wip:26:14 ]
    │
 26 │     for x in n {
    │              ┬  
    │              ╰── not an array, a slice or a buffer
    │ 
    │ Help: to count, walk a range: `for i in 0..n`
    │ 
    │ Note: a type of your own is walked when it lends its elements, `extend Deck: Items<Card>`, lends them one place at a time, `extend Ring: Sequence<Card>`, or hands them out one at a time, `extend Words: Iterator<str>`, which a generator writes for it: `fn words(): Iterator<str> = { … yield … }`
────╯
